// ADR-009 C3 #14 slice 4 (S4d) — EVALUATE-ONCE through the SUGAR (the S3c
// `warning[`-marker-count pattern, optional second cell): a COEXISTENCE
// definition carries a user `comptime post` handler with the observable
// marker (`warning("sugar-cfg-eval")`) BESIDE a declarative `before` hook
// (typed config ⇒ TypedConfig class ⇒ the S4c lowering appends its
// synthesized post handler AFTER the user handler — both run once per
// @application). The marker must appear EXACTLY twice on subprocess stderr
// (== the application count) in BOTH modes:
//   - once-globally would cap it at 1 (the two applications carry
//     structurally EQUAL config, so Dec-95 rule 6 SHARES one baked
//     specialization — the count follows APPLICATIONS, not
//     specializations);
//   - a per-invocation config eval would scale with the 200-call hot loop
//     (400+; the S0 §4 a4e legacy contrast).
//
// Hot loop of 200 iterations calls BOTH targets each pass (each target
// crosses T1@100). 1-ary Single-carrier targets, off the S2d
// aggregate-carrier gap (S7's named follow-up).
//
// Value-distinguishing arithmetic, per call i in 0..200 per target:
//   before: a0 = i * times = 3i;  impl: * 10 → 30i
//   total = 2 targets * 30 * 19900 = 1194000
// Expected stdout: 1194000
//   skipped before → 2 * 10 * 19900 = 398000
//   times misread as 1 → 2 * 10 * 19900 = 398000 (same as skip: *1 is identity)
//   one target unwoven → 30*19900 + 10*19900 = 796000
annotation traced(times: int) {
  targets: [function]
  comptime post(target, ctx) {
    warning("sugar-cfg-eval")
  }
  before(args) {
    args[0] = args[0] * times
    return args
  }
}

@traced(3)
fn calc_a(a: int) -> int { a * 10 }

@traced(3)
fn calc_b(a: int) -> int { a * 10 }

fn run() -> int {
  let mut total = 0
  for i in 0..200 { total = total + calc_a(i) + calc_b(i) }
  total
}
print(run())
